From 7ae39f87e7c9fd8c59241f604b9a65f4ae8f686d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:18:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: the channel picker keeps to channels every AiMesh node
 can use

The 5 GHz picker's own fall-back after a failed DFS check parked the owner's
radio on a channel the mesh node could not follow, inside the controller's
own exclusion list, for two hours, and nothing said that every remaining
node channel was DFS. rc/reaper_meshchan.c (pure block, compiled by the host
test) reads the AiMesh controller's per-unit channel lists
(/tmp/chanspec_all.json, 0000FCCC codes, under file_lock("chanspec")), fits
each radio to the sub-block every node can use, keeps the plan in
/jffs/reaper_meshchan/wlN.compat with a /tmp mirror, and hands the
exclusions to reaper_bwfloor's picker after the width floor. When the
exclusions in force leave the nodes no non-DFS channel at the floor, the
stock Auto-width exclusions every node can use are allowed again and
written through to the running picker (acs_cli2 set acs_excl_chans); a
radio found outside the plan for 60 s is moved to a node-usable non-DFS
chanspec (the Site Survey mechanism), three tries with a growing cooldown,
and held while a node is joining. amaspark reads the bss state through the
iovar instead of a fork. nvram amas_chanfit (default on; idle without a
node) with a switch on the Wireless page; the daemon stays up while it is
on (rwatch probe). Diag v1.3.40 adds the "node fit:" line.

Metal: owner RT-BE96U with an RT-AX92U node, MLO on - v3.4.5_BETA_r4: the
plan built within 20 s of the node's join, 149-161/80 allowed again;
_r9: the lifted chanspecs read Valid in acs_cli2's candidate dump and the
radio sits on 149/80, a channel the node can use. Lean:
tests/test_mesh_chanfit.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
